Verdict: ❌ Does not meet requirements

Pages & Structure: Only index.html and about.html provided. Missing gallery, setting, contact pages (hard requirement = 5 files).

Visual Accuracy: Layout is an approximation. Spacing, typography scale, borders, and proportions are not pixel-matched. Tailwind defaults mixed with custom CSS cause inconsistency.

HTML Quality: Excessive non-semantic <div> usage, duplicated headers across pages, placeholder links (#) in navigation.

CSS Quality: Very large, repetitive media queries (over-engineered). Many commented blocks, redundant rules, and inconsistent sizing strategy.

Responsiveness: Works across breakpoints, but relies on brute-force scaling instead of design fidelity.

Functionality: Mobile menu works. Search is purely visual (no logic). No gallery, settings, or contact functionality.

Accessibility: Minimal. No ARIA roles, no keyboard handling for menu, missing focus states, images without descriptive alt text.

Best Practices & SEO: Meta description and keywords present, but no author meta, no lazy loading, no noopener noreferrer, no integrity attributes.


Remark: Submission by Abdullah Shaikh shows strong effort and better technical depth than basic static attempts, but fails core requirements: missing pages, non–pixel-perfect execution, overcomplicated CSS, and incomplete production readiness.